Saint Lucia Population and Housing Census - 2022
Statement of Confidentiality
The information collected during the Population and Housing Census for 2022 is strictly confidential
and will not be divulged to a third party without the consent of the individual(s) who provided the data.
We want to assure census participants that extensive measures were taken to anonymize the names and
demographic particulars of everyone who provided information to the Central Statistical Office. The
collected data will not be shared with a third party if the information leads to respondents' direct or
indirect identification. Every census worker, including non-permanent employees of the Central
Statistics Office, is under an oath of secrecy and is criminally liable if in any form or manner
disseminates the information collected to a third party during or after the data collection exercise.
Mechanisms are built into the system to report potential breaches of census procedures and
confidentiality.
Legal Basis for the 2022 Census
A census is the primary source of information about a country's population and is conducted every 10
years at a minimum. Saint Lucia’s Central Statistical Office is mandated by the Statistics Act, Cap.
17.12 of the Laws of Saint Lucia, Section 3(1)(a) to conduct the Population and Housing Census.
According to Sections 2 and 5 of the Census Act, Cap. 17.02 of the Revised Laws of Saint Lucia, the
requisite order, and regulations were made to direct that a Census be taken for Saint Lucia and
subsequently gazette in the public journal of the government.
Improvements to the 2022 Census
The 2022 Census incorporated significant advancements in technological development, with a clear
focus on enhancing efficiency and data quality relative to previous censuses. The census leveraged
digital tools, including satellite imagery, essential for a comprehensive mapping and listing of all
structures and households. This process was further bolstered by adapting the WB Computer-Assisted
Personal Interview (CAPI) software where training and fieldwork materials were preloaded onto tablet
PCs, reducing the need for extensive printing of manuals and questionnaires.
The technologies used for the 2022 Census supported the recording of GPS coordinates of households,
enabling the integration of household locations with their associated social and economic facilities into
the system. GPS technology is recognized for enhancing census coverage by identifying omissions
during the mapping and listing phases. but also, to enable the validation of collected data. Two distinct
types of questionnaires were employed: the Household questionnaire, designed to gather information
on household characteristics, and the Person questionnaire, intended to capture individual
characteristics. While the content of the 2022 census questionnaires mirrored that of previous census
questionnaires, some modifications were made to address specific needs.
