Terms and Definitions
Term Definition
Age dependency ratio The age dependency ratio relates the number of children (0-14 years old) and
older persons (65 years or over) to the working-age population (15-64 years
old).
Building A building is an independent free-standing structure comprising one or more
rooms or other spaces, covered by a roof, and usually enclosed within external
walls or dividing walls from adjoining buildings that extend from the
foundations to the roof. A building may be a factory, shop, detached dwelling,
apartment building, warehouse, repair shop, poultry pen, etc. Detached rooms
relating to the main buildings are treated as part of the main building, for
example, detached kitchens, toilets, servants’ quarters, garages, etc.
Business A business is an activity that is carried on in a systematic, continuous, and
regular manner. It carries an expectation of financial return or profit, from
exchanging money for work, accepting risk, and selling goods and/or services.
Census night Point of reference for the census, usually the night just before the field count
begins. For the St. Lucia 2022 Census, this was the night between 12 and 13
March 2022. Respondents were asked to provide information about their
situation at that time.
“De facto” population The respondents are enumerated where they are found, regardless of their usual
place of residence
“De jure” population The respondents are enumerated at their usual place of residence, regardless of
where they stayed on census night.
Demographic Countries are going through a transition process in which the birth rate strongly
dividend decreases. At the same time, the number of older people is still relatively small
due to the former pyramid-like shape of the age-sex distribution. This
temporarily leads to a low dependency ratio, which countries may exploit to
improve their economic situation: the demographic dividend.
Dwelling A dwelling unit is any building or separate and independent part of a building
in which a person or group of persons is living at the time of the census
enumeration. There must be direct access from the street or common landing,
staircase, passage, or gallery where occupants can enter or leave without passing
through anybody else’s living quarters. A dwelling unit is one in which one or
several households reside. This may be a single house, flat, apartment, out-
room, part of a commercial building, or a boarding house catering for less than
six people.
Household A group of people related or unrelated, who live together in the same dwelling
unit and share living accommodations. This can include family members as well
as non-family members such as roommates
Institutional The institutional population comprises people who are not members of private
Population households. These include the residents of dormitories of schools and
universities, religious institutions, hospitals, and correctional and penal
institutions.
10
  == page 11 ==
Saint Lucia Population and Housing Census - 2022
Labour force The labour force, or economically active population, consists of the population
ages 15 and older that have worked at least one hour for pay, profit or family
gain over the last week for the census, plus those who have been actively looking
for work during this period.
Net migration rate Net migration rate compares the difference between the number of persons
entering and leaving a country during the year per 1,000 persons.
Number of inhabited The total count of buildings that are occupied and used as residences by people.
buildings This includes any structure where people live, such as houses, apartments, flats,
or other residential dwellings. The term helps to distinguish between buildings
that are used for habitation and those used for other purposes (e.g., commercial,
industrial, vacant, or abandoned buildings). The number of inhabited buildings
is an important statistic in understanding housing availability, population
distribution, and urban development within a given area.
Labour force The labour force participation rate is the proportion of the population ages 15
participation rate and older that is economically active.
Person 1 For census enumeration purposes, every private household must have a Person
1. In the past, this person was called Head of the household. It is the person
recognized from the household who is the main respondent. Since the notion of
Head of household is no longer broadly supported, the role of Person 1 can be
assigned to any responsible adult in the household.
Population and A population and housing census involves a comprehensive process of planning,
Housing Census collecting, compiling, evaluating, disseminating, and analyzing demographic,
economic, and social data at the smallest geographic level at a specific time. Its
goal is to account for all individuals in a country and the condition of all housing
units and facilities available to households. This data is crucial for economic
and social development, administrative activities, and scientific research, as it
provides reliable and detailed information on the population's size, distribution,
and composition. The census also includes information on homeless individuals
and gathers sufficient demographic, social, and economic data to describe
housing conditions and analyze housing deficiencies for potential remedial
actions.
Post-enumeration The purpose of a post-enumeration survey is to measure the accuracy of a
survey census. The survey determines the quality of the census by independently
surveying a sample of the population.
Private household A household consists of one or more persons living together, sleeping in the
same dwelling most nights, and sharing at least one daily meal. A member of a
household need not be a relative of the main family. For example, a boarder or
a domestic servant who sleeps in most nights of the week is considered a
member of the household. A household can consist of just one person, or of
more than one family if they share living arrangements. A group of unrelated
persons living together can also comprise a household.
Sex ratio The number of males per 100 females.
