Saint Lucia Labour Force
Tables D.8-D.12 provide a detailed overview of the current state of the labour market including labour
force, employment, and unemployment in Saint Lucia, drawing comparisons with census data from
2010 to illustrate key trends and areas of future focus (Table D.11). The labour market in Saint Lucia
has shown notable improvement from 2010 to 2022 (Table 16). The unemployment rate has decreased
significantly, and the number of employed individuals has increased (Table 15). Despite this positive
trend, certain age groups, particularly the youth continue to face high unemployment rates (Table D.9).
Gender disparities in unemployment are minimal, with males and females experiencing similar rates
across most age groups. The ten districts show variations in unemployment rates, with Canaries
experiencing the highest rate and Gros Islet the lowest (Table D.12). Based on the census information,
Saint Lucia can boast a growing and dynamic labour force with substantial increases in overall
employment and workforce participation. The unemployment rate has decreased markedly, indicating
positive strides toward economic stability and improved livelihoods for Saints Lucians.
